{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03115",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 4.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.4,
      "end_seconds": 13.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Hi doctor, you know, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.05,
      "end_seconds": 19.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.23,
      "end_seconds": 28.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "So, of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 28.72,
      "end_seconds": 33.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "We came because of a sudden severe tummy pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.12,
      "end_seconds": 36.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.35,
      "end_seconds": 50.89,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "I'd say about three months. Actually, no, closer to about a month. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.44,
      "end_seconds": 53.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.16,
      "end_seconds": 62.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Uh, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.61,
      "end_seconds": 70.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.92,
      "end_seconds": 89.76,
      "duration_seconds": 17.84,
      "text": "I, I'd say a couple of times a week. As for shoulder tip pain, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.26,
      "end_seconds": 97.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Okay, have you had a sudden severe tummy pain before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.34,
      "end_seconds": 104.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.89,
      "end_seconds": 107.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Did you notice any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.05,
      "end_seconds": 109.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.11,
      "end_seconds": 117.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Okay, any diarrhoea or blood in the vomit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.27,
      "end_seconds": 131.8,
      "duration_seconds": 13.53,
      "text": "No, no diarrhoea, no blood in the vomit. I did have vomiting at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.31,
      "end_seconds": 135.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.39,
      "end_seconds": 138.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.51,
      "end_seconds": 141.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.24,
      "end_seconds": 150.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Let me think, I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.38,
      "end_seconds": 157.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.25,
      "end_seconds": 163.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Alendronate, 70 milligrams, maybe, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.9,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.86,
      "end_seconds": 183.59,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so not with me. I'll bring it next time. I take Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 185.43,
      "end_seconds": 193.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "It's meant to be every morning, though I don't see he take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.32,
      "end_seconds": 201.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Atorvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.53,
      "end_seconds": 212.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "It's a... um, um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.25,
      "end_seconds": 217.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Alright, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.81,
      "end_seconds": 229.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "For the gout, I believe. My son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.17,
      "end_seconds": 234.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.74,
      "end_seconds": 238.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.12,
      "end_seconds": 243.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "So, a few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.0,
      "end_seconds": 260.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.55,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I gave up cigarettes last spring. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.92,
      "end_seconds": 264.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.03,
      "end_seconds": 295.93,
      "duration_seconds": 29.9,
      "text": "I've got thin bones. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've, I've got an underactive thyroid. High cholesterol, for about ten years. Right, um, I've had gout for about ten years now. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. Well, you know, I have diabetes, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.94,
      "end_seconds": 309.45,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol and gout are known to us, good to have that clear. Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.23,
      "end_seconds": 315.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 316.7,
      "end_seconds": 329.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 111 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18. SpO2 96 percent on room air, temperature 36.6, pressure 133 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.33,
      "end_seconds": 331.03,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.68,
      "end_seconds": 335.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.2,
      "end_seconds": 339.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.47,
      "end_seconds": 359.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Your tummy is rigid like a board and very tender everywhere, and you are lying completely still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.21,
      "end_seconds": 366.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.91,
      "end_seconds": 416.99,
      "duration_seconds": 32.08,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? This looks most like a perforated stomach ulcer. Another possibility is pancreatitis. I'd like to arrange an erect chest X-ray for possible perforation. Urgent blood tests is what I'd like next, for acute abdomen. I'd like to arrange a CT scan for possible perforation. Nothing to eat or drink, you need an operation urgently. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 418.39,
      "end_seconds": 431.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.32,
      "end_seconds": 436.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Alright, uh, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 437.47,
      "end_seconds": 443.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "I'll want another look straight away. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.62,
      "end_seconds": 446.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.45,
      "end_seconds": 450.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Right, see you soon."
    }
  ]
}